WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.159
(light music)

00:00:04.409 --> 00:00:06.569
- So you wanna be a landlord?

00:00:06.569 --> 00:00:08.383
Great. You're at the right spot.

00:00:08.383 --> 00:00:11.055
Well, let me tell you, being
a landlord isn't an easy job

00:00:11.055 --> 00:00:13.432
like fire fighting or being a governor.

00:00:13.432 --> 00:00:15.058
Being a landlord takes training

00:00:15.058 --> 00:00:16.693
and I'm here to give you the training

00:00:16.693 --> 00:00:19.607
so you can succeed and get
the praise that you deserve.

00:00:19.607 --> 00:00:22.116
When a new tenant is
putting down their deposit,

00:00:22.116 --> 00:00:25.153
make sure they pay in a
money order, never a check.

00:00:25.153 --> 00:00:26.812
Checks are too easy.

00:00:26.812 --> 00:00:28.912
Money orders tiptoe the
line between ridiculous

00:00:28.912 --> 00:00:31.574
and inconvenient, so they're perfect.

00:00:31.574 --> 00:00:32.874
Now, before your tenant moves in,

00:00:32.874 --> 00:00:35.119
make sure the apartment isn't at 100%.

00:00:35.119 --> 00:00:37.923
You know, a wobbly knob
here, a leaky faucet there,

00:00:37.923 --> 00:00:39.335
anything you can do

00:00:39.335 --> 00:00:41.451
to make sure you get the security deposit,

00:00:41.451 --> 00:00:44.719
or what we like to call
in the biz as free money.

00:00:44.719 --> 00:00:47.432
Never answer a phone call from a tenant.

00:00:47.432 --> 00:00:49.849
Whenever a tenant calls
you, they want two things.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.729
They either want you to fix something

00:00:51.729 --> 00:00:53.752
or they want to tell you something stupid

00:00:53.752 --> 00:00:54.847
like there was just a burglary

00:00:54.847 --> 00:00:56.717
and you don't need that
stress in your life.

00:00:56.717 --> 00:00:58.891
The only time you should
speak to a tenant on the phone

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:01.392
is when you call them
up at 6 AM on a Saturday

00:01:01.392 --> 00:01:03.645
to tell them, hey, in
two Wednesdays from now,

00:01:03.645 --> 00:01:05.575
I'm shutting off the
water for maintenance.

00:01:05.575 --> 00:01:07.109
Which brings me to my next step.

00:01:07.109 --> 00:01:10.065
Every few months, just shut
the water off for maintenance.

00:01:10.065 --> 00:01:11.823
What does maintenance mean?

00:01:11.823 --> 00:01:14.830
I don't know, but the power
of telling your tenant

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.664
when they can and can't
shower is just incredible,

00:01:17.664 --> 00:01:18.873
so use that power.

00:01:18.873 --> 00:01:21.209
You also have the power of eviction.

00:01:21.209 --> 00:01:23.424
Every once in a while,
knock on their door and say,

00:01:23.424 --> 00:01:25.081
hey, you've been a little loud lately

00:01:25.081 --> 00:01:26.832
or just ask if you can have a look around

00:01:26.832 --> 00:01:29.428
because this is your
property, you control it.

00:01:29.428 --> 00:01:31.053
Own that power.

00:01:31.053 --> 00:01:33.603
After your tenant has been
in the unit for about a year,

00:01:33.603 --> 00:01:36.478
hike the rent up by 200
dollars, just for funsies.

00:01:36.478 --> 00:01:38.144
It'll throw them off an confuse them,

00:01:38.144 --> 00:01:40.145
so you just did your job.

00:01:40.145 --> 00:01:42.400
If your tenant decides to
leave your unit for elsewhere,

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.280
make sure to inspect that thing

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.322
for every little possible flaw.

00:01:46.322 --> 00:01:49.278
You know, a wobbly knob
here, a leaky faucet there.

00:01:49.278 --> 00:01:51.239
Anything to secure that free money

00:01:51.239 --> 00:01:53.575
because that's the end game.

00:01:53.575 --> 00:01:55.028
If you follow these steps,

00:01:55.028 --> 00:01:56.999
I can guarantee you will feel fulfilled.

00:01:56.999 --> 00:01:59.040
Remember, you are a landlord.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.422
They expect you to be annoying,

00:02:00.422 --> 00:02:02.379
inconvenient, and mysterious.

00:02:03.825 --> 00:02:06.960
(light music)

